he insurance example doesn't justify your caution. It actually reveals how our society draws a bright line: anonymous risk management for insurers, constrained by anti-discrimination principles, versus human decency, which requires treating people as individuals when we have every reason to know better. You have every reason to know better about your colleague. The only caution warranted is the caution against unfairness.
